      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2017 Elsevier Masson SAS. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "In the case of end-stage heart failure, the medical-surgical team can suggest the use of an external circulatory assist device as a definitive therapy. Living with this assistance requires a certain amount of adaptation on the part of the patients and their family, but can significantly improve quality of life. Support groups give them the opportunity to talk about their new life and receive psychological support."
      },
